Everything the C work checks against.

**Done when:**
- a throwaway Python venv in the session scratchpad has transformers and sentence-transformers, and runs both models;
- gte-modernbert-base and gte-reranker-modernbert-base are in kb's format in `~/.kb/models` (only model files, only that folder). A converter script lives in the repo, so anyone can reproduce the files from the Hugging Face weights, with the source revision and SHA-256 recorded;
- the facts the C code needs are written down from the real configs: tokenizer (BPE merges, specials, normalisation), layers, heads, local and global attention pattern and window, RoPE bases, activations, norms, pooling, query/document prefixes if any, and the classifier head;
- reference outputs (tokens, embeddings, reranker scores) for a fixed set of texts are saved as test fixtures.

**Done when:**
- a doc query set (150+) over this repository's docs and a code query set (100+) over its code (C, TypeScript, and more as they are indexed), each tagged paraphrase / identifier / purpose, with one to three right sections each. Candidates may be drafted by an agent; every label is checked;
- a harness (kept out of the default test run) builds a store from a pinned list of files, then runs keyword, semantic and hybrid (and later reranked) search. It reports hit@1, hit@3 and MRR@10 per mode and per tag, with bootstrap 95% intervals;
