kb is fast on small stores. Its costs grow with document size and store size in a few known places. Measure them first, then fix the ones that matter.

Known from the performance review (2026-09-26):
- embedding runs at about 0.58 s per chunk, so a 300-page PDF takes minutes and can exceed an agent's tool timeout;
- every hybrid search is a new process that maps the model file and embeds the query;
- every add rebuilds the keyword index from the whole store;
- the graph view's force layout compares every pair of nodes at each step, on the webview's main thread;
- vector search compares against every chunk, which is fine to around 100k chunks.
